    "url": "https://rift-ds.com/docs/schemas",
    "title": "/docs/schemas",
    "heading": "/docs/schemas",
    "body": "The index of every component schema\nThe meta-schema each component schema validates against\nThe meta-schema the index validates against\nThe tokens, one file per theme and mode (DTCG)\nThe tokens resolved per theme, in the package\nThe meta-schema the token values validate against\nThe prop name. Native attributes pass through every component and are not listed; only the component's own props are.\nThe resolved TypeScript type as text, literal unions expanded.\nThe shape of the type, so a reader can branch without parsing TypeScript: enum, primitive, array, function, reference or other.\nThe members of a literal union, present exactly when typeKind is enum. A prop typed through a named alias gets its members here too.\nWhether the prop must be passed.\nThe prop's JSDoc description, present on every own prop by build rule.\nThe default as a value: a number, a boolean, null, an enum member, or a string literal.\nAny other default as source text: a function, a computed number, a template string or a reference to another prop.\nSet when the prop carries a deprecation: the replacement guidance. The prop still works, because the published API only grows.\nThe types in the file's types map that the prop's type names, so one prop's types can be read without the rest.\nEvery component and token as a file a program can read\nGenerated on every build, so they always match what the package ships. For one component, use the For agents button on its page.\nEach component schema is a closed contract. Every type its props name is defined under types, nested types included, or named under externalTypes with the package that defines it, such as ReactNode from React.\nWhat a prop holds in a component schema\nThe fields of a prop in a component schema\nIn code, rift-ds/tokens/values gives every token's value for every theme in light and dark.\nFor design tools such as Figma, Style Dictionary or Tokens Studio, the same tokens are DTCG files under /schema/tokens/, one per theme and mode, with semantic tokens kept as aliases of their primitives."
