    "body": "Data visualisation components for plotting series and activity over time.\n\n- Area chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/area-chart): Filled area chart for showing volume over time, with stacked and single-series variants.\n- Bar chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/bar-chart): Vertical bars for comparing values across categories or time, with summary stats and tooltips.\n- Combo chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/combo-chart): Bar and line series in one chart, with an optional second y-axis for pairs in different units, like spend and ROAS.\n- Contribution graph (https://rift-ds.com/components/contribution-graph): A year of activity, one cell per day.\n- Funnel chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/funnel-chart): Ordered funnel stages as centred trapezoid bands, each sized by its share of the first stage.\n- Gantt chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/gantt-chart): Phases and tasks as bars on a shared timeline, with milestones, progress, and a today rule.\n- Gauge (https://rift-ds.com/components/gauge): A radial dial for a single bounded reading, recoloured through the status roles as it crosses thresholds.\n- Legend tile (https://rift-ds.com/components/legend-tile): The labelled value tile under a chart: a series dot, the series name, and its reading, on a soft neutral fill.\n- Line chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/line-chart): Multi-series line chart for trends over time, with per-series colours and a summary row.\n- Pie chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/pie-chart): Proportional share of a whole as a pie or donut, with per-slice colours.\n- Radar chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/radar-chart): Multi-axis comparison of series across categories on a radial grid.\n- Radial chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/radial-chart): Concentric progress rings for completion and KPI readouts.\n- Scatter chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/scatter-chart): Plots point clusters across two axes to show correlation and distribution.\n- Sparkline (https://rift-ds.com/components/sparkline): Inline trend line for stats and table cells, drawn without axes or chrome.\n- Stacked bar chart (https://rift-ds.com/components/stacked-bar-chart): Bars split into stacked segments to compare totals and their composition.\n- Treemap (https://rift-ds.com/components/treemap): Nested rectangles sized by value for part-to-whole breakdowns."
