    "heading": "Components › Data display",
    "body": "Cards, tables, lists, and badges for presenting structured content.\n\n- Accordion (https://rift-ds.com/components/accordion): Collapsible content sections for organising related information.\n- Animated number (https://rift-ds.com/components/animated-number): A number that counts to its value: count-up on mount, eased tweens on change, tabular digits that never jitter.\n- Avatar (https://rift-ds.com/components/avatar): User profile image with initials and icon fallback, status indicator, and multiple sizes.\n- Avatar group (https://rift-ds.com/components/avatar-group): Overlapping avatar stack with a +N counter for the overflow.\n- Badge (https://rift-ds.com/components/badge): Small inline status labels with info, positive, warning, error, and neutral variants.\n- Bento tile (https://rift-ds.com/components/bento-tile): A feature tile for a bento grid, with a safe content area, a shader pair, solid or transparent background, and an overlay it opens into.\n- Card (https://rift-ds.com/components/card): A titled preview tile for index grids, with a case-study variant carrying a cover, company logo and dek.\n- Card stack (https://rift-ds.com/components/card-stack): A deck of cards showing one at a time, flipped through with a lift-and-settle animation.\n- Carousel (https://rift-ds.com/components/carousel): Sliding content viewer with navigation arrows, dot indicators, auto-play, and keyboard support.\n- Chip (https://rift-ds.com/components/chip): Compact pills for attributes, filters, and inline metadata.\n- Code block (https://rift-ds.com/components/code-block): Monospace code with a header and one-click copy.\n- Contact card (https://rift-ds.com/components/contact-card): Linked contact method with icon, label, and value.\n- Data table (https://rift-ds.com/components/data-table): The wired table: typed columns, sorting, filters, editing, grouping with totals, row details, saved views, thousands of rows, and rows from a server.\n- Deadline (https://rift-ds.com/components/deadline): A due date against now that turns from neutral to warning to error as it nears.\n- Description list (https://rift-ds.com/components/description-list): Terms and their values for review screens, receipts, and account details, stacked, in two columns, or in a grid.\n- Document viewer (https://rift-ds.com/components/document-viewer): A PDF, an image or a text file shown on the page, with download and a fallback where the browser will not embed it.\n- Entity card (https://rift-ds.com/components/entity-card): Compact display-only card with a centred icon or image and a label, used in the Icons and Logos galleries.\n- Event calendar (https://rift-ds.com/components/event-calendar): A month grid with event pills, overflow counts, and month navigation.\n- Figure (https://rift-ds.com/components/figure): Images with captions, in the case-study frame.\n- Image compare (https://rift-ds.com/components/image-compare): Before-and-after image comparison with a draggable divider, keyboard control, and corner labels.\n- Instructions (https://rift-ds.com/components/instructions): Step-by-step guidance with numbered badges, connecting lines, and horizontal layout.\n- Kbd (https://rift-ds.com/components/kbd): A keyboard key rendered as a keycap, for shortcut hints in menus and prose.\n- Link list (https://rift-ds.com/components/link-list): Linked items with logo, label, and subtitle.\n- Pixel avatar (https://rift-ds.com/components/pixel-avatar): A generated character mark drawn from a name: the same name is always the same pixel creature in the same ink.\n- Quote (https://rift-ds.com/components/quote): Blockquotes and pull-quotes with attribution.\n- Selection card (https://rift-ds.com/components/selection-card): Large option cards for high-visibility choices like settings and onboarding, with radio, checkbox or per-card toggle indicators.\n- Stat (https://rift-ds.com/components/stat): Headline metrics with labels and trend deltas.\n- Table (https://rift-ds.com/components/table): Data table with flexible cell content, striped rows, compact sizing, and support for icons, inputs, buttons, and interactive controls.\n- Table toolbar (https://rift-ds.com/components/table-toolbar): The control bar over a table: search, filter chips, sort, group, columns, density, saved views and a bulk bar, wired to a DataTable in its toolbar slot.\n- Timeline (https://rift-ds.com/components/timeline): Ordered sequences: histories and steppers.\n- Tree view (https://rift-ds.com/components/tree-view): Collapsible hierarchy for files, folders, and nested structures.\n- Widget (https://rift-ds.com/components/widget): A titled section for a dashboard, a form, or settings, with rows, groups, a footer, an optional fold, and a board of columns."
