    "heading": "1.2.0: The Inspector family",
    "body": "Six one-row controls for tool panels and settings rails: InspectorSlider, InspectorInput, InspectorToggleSwitch, InspectorSegmentedControl, InspectorDropdown, and InspectorSection to group them. Each is one bar with its name inside, sized and shaped like Button, so a dense panel of settings stays light. They sit beside the form controls rather than replacing them.\n\nSegmentedControl's track corner now counts its hairline, so on a theme with squarer pills it stays parallel with the sliding pill. Nothing breaks, so upgrading needs no code changes.",
