    "heading": "1.1.0: Mobile app navigation",
    "body": "Three new navigation components. BottomNav is the tab bar of a mobile app, drawn in the Rift style, as the iOS Liquid Glass capsule, or as the Material 3 Expressive bar. TopAppBar is the header of a mobile screen, with a title that collapses as the page scrolls. SidebarPanel lists one section's pages, on its own or beside AppSidebar as a third navigation level.\n\nScreen readers get more to work with: charts are named by their title, Nav names its landmark and accepts native props, and Stepper announces its steps. Nothing breaks, so upgrading needs no code changes.",
